# Repository Agent Notes

This repository is a gem5 fork on the `kui-dev` line. The local work is focused
on integrating a KuiLoong NPU SAU (Systolic Array Unit) model into gem5.

## Current Focus

- Main gem5 SimObject work lives in `src/sau`.
- The active gem5 model is `KuiSau`, with a supporting CSR traffic generator
  `CsrGen` and deterministic golden driver `SauGoldenGen`.
- `src/sau/SConscript` is the build entry for the current gem5-facing SAU code.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_system_mem.py` is the simple memory-connectivity
  smoke test used in `docs/my_gem5.md`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_test.py` is the first deterministic
  SAU functional-output test.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_add_test.py` covers a deterministic
  matrix-add output vector using `SauGoldenGen(test_case="add")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_shift_test.py` covers a deterministic
  shift-mode GEMM vector using `SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_shift")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_test.py` covers a deterministic
  cutbit/dequantization vector using `SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant")`;
  the golden run now passes.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_negative_test.py` covers a
  deterministic negative cutbit/dequantization vector using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant_negative")`; the golden run now passes.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_int16_test.py` covers a
  deterministic int16 cutbit/dequantization vector using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant_int16")`; the golden run now passes.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_pointwise_test.py` covers a
  deterministic pointwise-convolution vector using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="pointwise")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_pointwise_dequant_mixed_test.py`
  covers a deterministic pointwise `work_mode=2` mixed-sign dequantization
  vector using `SauGoldenGen(test_case="pointwise_dequant_mixed")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_transpose_test.py` covers a
  deterministic output-transpose vector using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_out_transpose")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_test.py` covers a
  deterministic normal-convolution vector using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv")`; the golden run now passes.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_rich_test.py` covers a
  deterministic normal-convolution rich-data vector with multiple signed A lanes
  and distinct signed B kernel rows using
  `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_rich")`.
- `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_shift_test.py` covers a
