Latest completed slice: first RTL `mem_addr.sv` formula pass is recorded.
`SA_CORE.sv` sets `BASE_ADDR=0x20000000`, matching gem5 golden memory. RTL
`csr.sv` maps word 2 horizontal=B and vertical=A, and word 3 bias=C and
output=D, so the logical tags line up after renaming. RTL output D addressing
matches the current gem5 summary shape for default `x_step=1` and
`channel_step=1`, including shift-mode adjacent `+16` rows. Known request-trace
gaps before claiming RTL equivalence: RTL only issues bias/C reads when
`pe_work_mode == SA_pkg::CONV` (`work_mode=1`), while `SAU.py` and gem5 enable
C for normal/DW conv regardless of work mode; and RTL scheduler ordering may
read horizontal/B before vertical/A, while gem5 currently batches tagged
A/B/C requests by kind.

Latest completed slice: C/bias request gating is now selectable. `KuiSau.py`
adds `rtl_c_read_gate` (default `False`), and `KuiSau` uses it to keep default
functional runs aligned with `SAU.py` while allowing RTL-style C/bias reads only
when `work_mode == 1`. Added
`configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_rtl_trace_test.py`
as a trace-oriented normal-conv stride check. Verified build:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev scons build/RISCV/gem5.opt -j2`.
Default run
`m5out/sau_addr_normal_conv_stride_default_cgate` still reads C and reports
12 read segments with C first/last/sum/xor
`536879104/536879120/1073758224/16`. RTL-gated run
`m5out/sau_addr_normal_conv_stride_rtl_cgate` passes the same D output check,
reports 10 read segments, and reports C first/last/sum/xor `0/0/0/0`. A/B/D
summaries match between both runs.

Latest completed slice: RTL-gated representative address-summary coverage has
been widened. Added trace configs for `normal_conv_stride_shift`, `pointwise`,
and `gemm_shift`:
`configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_shift_rtl_trace_test.py`,
`configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_pointwise_rtl_trace_test.py`, and
`configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_shift_rtl_trace_test.py`. Verified runs:
`m5out/sau_addr_normal_conv_stride_shift_rtl_cgate`,
`m5out/sau_addr_pointwise_rtl_cgate`, and
`m5out/sau_addr_gemm_shift_rtl_cgate`. All three D output checks passed and the
stats matched expected summaries. Stride+shift RTL-gated drops C to `0/0/0/0`
and reports 16 read segments. Pointwise `work_mode=1` keeps C at
`536879104/536879120/1073758224/16` and reports 34 read segments. GEMM shift
