the four `util/sau_trace_summary.py --case ... --gem5-stats ...` checks for
the RTL-gated representative runs, and both sample RTL CSV parse modes
(`/tmp/sau_monitor_sample.csv` and `/tmp/sau_monitor_infer_sample.csv`).

Latest completed slice: per-kind request counts are now part of both gem5 stats
and the trace summary checker. `KuiSau` records `flowReadARequests`,
`flowReadBRequests`, `flowReadCRequests`, and `flowWriteDRequests`.
`util/sau_trace_summary.py` prints and compares those fields, and now has a
fixed external RTL smoke case named `lkssfull_sau_stdconv_10`. Verified:
`python3 util/sau_trace_summary.py --case lkssfull_sau_stdconv_10 --rtl-trace /home/zbn/code/npu_lpnpu/sim/vcs/build/mikui_dma/sau_mem_addr_trace.csv`,
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev scons build/RISCV/gem5.opt -j2`, reruns
of the four RTL-gated gem5 representative cases into `m5out/sau_order_*`, and
their `util/sau_trace_summary.py --case ... --gem5-stats ...` checks. The four
representative gem5 counts are normal-conv stride A/B/C/D `6/4/0/16`,
normal-conv stride+shift `12/4/0/32`, pointwise `16/16/2/16`, and gemm-shift
`32/16/0/32`.

Latest completed slice: `util/sau_trace_summary.py` now has `--show-flows`.
The tool preserves optional RTL cycle numbers while keeping existing built-in
case generation compatible, splits a trace after each D-write run, and prints
per-flow cycles, request-kind run order, counts, and first/last addresses.
Verified on
`/home/zbn/code/npu_lpnpu/sim/vcs/build/mikui_dma/sau_mem_addr_trace.csv`:
`python3 util/sau_trace_summary.py --case lkssfull_sau_stdconv_10 --rtl-trace /home/zbn/code/npu_lpnpu/sim/vcs/build/mikui_dma/sau_mem_addr_trace.csv --show-flows`
passes the fixed summary and prints 16 flows. Each flow has 223 requests with
counts `A=127, B=62, C=2, D=32`; the run order is `B,A,C,A,D`, because each
flow has one final A read at `0x20025040` after the two C/bias reads and before
D writes. Existing gem5 summary checks still pass for `normal_conv_stride`,
`normal_conv_stride_shift`, `pointwise`, and `gemm_shift`.

Latest completed slice: output-retain conversion now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_retain")` runs two GEMM instructions in one
simulation: the first uses `flow_mode=2` and writes normal GEMM bytes while
retaining `D_matrix`; the second uses normal `flow_mode=0`, accumulates on the
retained matrix, and writes doubled bytes `[0, 2, 4, ..., 30]` in every row
before clearing. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_retain ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_retain_test.py`.
Retain stats: 16 CSR writes, 28 CSR reads, 2 flow starts/completions, 64 read
segments, 32 D write segments, and 486002 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: combined output-transpose plus retain now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_transpose_retain")` runs a first GEMM with
`flow_mode=3`, checks the same transposed bytes as `gemm_out_transpose`, then
runs a normal GEMM and checks doubled normal bytes to prove the untransposed
retained D state survived. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_transpose_retain ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_transpose_retain_test.py`.
Transpose-retain stats: 16 CSR writes, 28 CSR reads, 2 flow starts/completions,
64 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 486002 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: GEMM dequantization now has a deterministic vector.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant")` writes `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, uses
all-one A rows and B bytes `0, 4, 8, ..., 60`, and checks output bytes
`0, 16, 32, ..., 112, 127, ..., 127`; this covers right-shift dequantization
plus int8 saturation. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_dequant ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_test.py`.
Dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion, 32 read
segments, 16 D write segments, and 243001 busy ticks. A follow-up
`gemm_shift` recheck also passed at
`m5out/sau_golden_shift_recheck`.

Latest completed slice: negative GEMM dequantization now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant_negative")` writes `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`,
uses all-one A rows and B bytes encoding `0, -4, -8, ..., -60`, and checks
packed output bytes `0, 240, 224, ..., 144, 128, ..., 128`; this covers
arithmetic right shift plus negative int8 saturation. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_dequant_negative ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_negative_test.py`.
Negative dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion,
32 read segments, 16 D write segments, and 243001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: int16 GEMM dequantization now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="gemm_dequant_int16")` combines `shift_mode=1` with
`INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, reuses the int16 identity A layout from `gemm_shift`, and
checks the same int16 output byte ordering with each value right-shifted by 2.
Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_dequant_int16 ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_dequant_int16_test.py`.
Int16 dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 19 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion,
48 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 339001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: pointwise mixed-sign dequantization now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="pointwise_dequant_mixed")` uses `conv_kernel=1`,
`work_mode=2`, `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, identity A, alternating signed B columns,
and all-one C bias. It checks that C is shifted into accumulator scale before
the signed dequantized int8 output is packed. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_pointwise_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_pointwise_dequant_mixed_test.py`.
Pointwise mixed dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow
start/completion, 34 read segments, 16 D write segments, and 249001 busy
ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal-convolution mixed-sign dequantization now
passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_dequant_mixed")` uses
`conv_kernel=2`, `register_mode=0`, `work_mode=2`, `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, a
one-hot A tile, alternating signed B columns, and all-one C bias. It checks
normal-conv staging together with C scaling and signed int8 dequantized output
packing. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_dequant_mixed_test.py`.
Normal-conv mixed dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 11 CSR reads, 1 flow
start/completion, 10 read segments, 16 D write segments, and 177001 busy
ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal-convolution shift-mode output packing now
passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_shift")` uses `conv_kernel=2`,
`register_mode=0`, `shift_mode=1`, `flow_loop_times=2`, a one-hot A tile,
zero C data, and the fixed B row pattern. It checks the conv `int16`
`convMatShift` path plus SAU.py-style 512-byte D output packing. Verified
command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_shift ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_shift_test.py`.
Normal-conv shift stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion,
14 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 237001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: depthwise-convolution shift-mode output packing now
passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_shift")` uses
`conv_kernel=2`, `register_mode=2`, `shift_mode=1`, `flow_loop_times=2`, a
one-hot A tile, zero C data, and the fixed B row pattern. It checks the conv
`int16` `convMatShift` path, DW B-column mask, and SAU.py-style 512-byte D
output packing. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_shift ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_shift_test.py`.
Depthwise-conv shift stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow
start/completion, 14 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 237001 busy
ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal/depthwise convolution stride-mode output-row
selection now passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_stride")` and
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_stride")` both use `conv_kernel=2`,
`stride=1`, `shift_mode=0`, `flow_loop_times=1`, zero C data, and a one-hot A
lane in input row 1. The normal-conv vector checks that the fixed B row pattern
moves to D row 8; the depthwise vector checks that the DW B-column mask leaves
only byte 15 of D row 8 set. Verified commands:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_stride ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_test.py`
and
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_test.py`.
Both stride stats: 8 CSR writes, 11 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion, 12 read
segments, 16 D write segments, and 183001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal/depthwise combined stride+shift convolution now
passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_stride_shift")` and
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_stride_shift")` both use
`conv_kernel=2`, `stride=1`, `shift_mode=1`, `flow_loop_times=2`, zero C data,
and a one-hot A lane in input row 1. The normal-conv vector checks the stride
merge together with the 512-byte int16 D packing by producing nonzero packed
bytes in output rows 8/9; the depthwise vector checks that the DW B-column mask
still leaves only byte 15 of output row 8 set. Verified commands:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_shift ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_shift_test.py`
and
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_shift ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_shift_test.py`.
Both stride+shift stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion,
18 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 249001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal/depthwise combined stride+dequant convolution
now passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_stride_dequant_mixed")` and
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_stride_dequant_mixed")` both use
`conv_kernel=2`, `stride=1`, `shift_mode=0`, `work_mode=2`, `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`,
an input-row-1 one-hot A lane, alternating signed B columns, and all-one C
bias. The normal-conv vector proves stride row selection composes with C scaling
and signed dequantization by updating output row 8; the depthwise vector proves
the same path under the DW B-column mask. Verified commands:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_dequant_mixed_test.py`
and
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_dequant_mixed_test.py`.
Both stride+dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 11 CSR reads, 1 flow start/completion,
12 read segments, 16 D write segments, and 183001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: normal/depthwise combined stride+shift+dequant
convolution now passes.
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="normal_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed")` and
`SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed")` both use
`conv_kernel=2`, `stride=1`, `shift_mode=1`, `work_mode=2`,
`INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, `flow_loop_times=2`, an input-row-1 one-hot A lane,
alternating signed B columns, and all-one C bias. The normal-conv vector checks
stride row selection plus 512-byte int16 output packing after C scaling and
signed dequantization by updating packed D rows 8/9. The depthwise vector checks
the same combined path under the DW B-column mask by leaving only the expected
packed byte pair in row 8 changed from the unit-bias baseline. Verified
commands:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_normal_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed_test.py`
and
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_stride_shift_dequant_mixed_test.py`.
Both stride+shift+dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 14 CSR reads, 1 flow
start/completion, 18 read segments, 32 D write segments, and 249001 busy ticks.

Latest completed slice: depthwise-convolution mixed-sign dequantization now
passes. `SauGoldenGen(test_case="depthwise_conv_dequant_mixed")` uses
`conv_kernel=2`, `register_mode=2`, `work_mode=2`, `INS1_MSB.cutbit=2`, a
one-hot A tile, alternating signed B columns, and all-one C bias. It checks the
DW B-column mask together with C scaling and signed int8 dequantized output
packing. Verified command:
`docker exec -w /gem5/gem5-kui gem5-dev ./build/RISCV/gem5.opt --outdir=m5out/sau_golden_depthwise_conv_dequant_mixed ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_depthwise_conv_dequant_mixed_test.py`.
Depthwise-conv mixed dequant stats: 8 CSR writes, 11 CSR reads, 1 flow
start/completion, 10 read segments, 16 D write segments, and 177001 busy
ticks.

## Reference Sources

Reference material extracted from the KuiLoong NPU repositories is stored under
`src/sau/reference`. These files are not included by `src/sau/SConscript`.

- Hardware source repository: `/home/zbn/code/npu_lpnpu`
- Hardware extraction filelist:
  `/home/zbn/code/npu_lpnpu/syn/script/mikui_dma/lpnpu_mikui_dma.f`
- Reduced local SAU filelist:
  `src/sau/reference/hardware/lpnpu_mikui_dma_sau.f`
- Software simulator source:
  `/home/zbn/code/toolchain_workdir/workdir/gitee_toolchain/kuiloong-sim/src/SAU`
- Local simulator copy:
  `src/sau/reference/simulator/SAU/SAU.py`

The hardware extraction follows the SAU section of the source filelist:
`hardware/src/sa_execute`, `hardware/src/sa_element`, `macro.svh`, and
`SA_pkg.sv`. The local copy also includes `macro_gclk.svh`,
`v_clock_latch.v`, and `v_clock_pass.v` because `SA_CORE.sv` depends on them.
Python cache files from the simulator source were intentionally omitted.

## Useful Commands

Build the RISCV gem5 binary:

```sh
scons build/RISCV/gem5.opt -j$(nproc)
```

Run the current simple memory smoke test:

```sh
./build/RISCV/gem5.opt ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_system_mem.py > output.log
```

Run the focused CSR readback test:

```sh
./build/RISCV/gem5.opt ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_csrgen_test.py
```

Run the deterministic SAU golden GEMM test:

```sh
./build/RISCV/gem5.opt ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_test.py
```

Run the deterministic SAU matrix-add golden test:

```sh
./build/RISCV/gem5.opt ./configs/tutorial/part1/kui_sau_golden_add_test.py
```

Run the deterministic SAU shift-mode GEMM golden test:

```sh
