  `minsys_uart.log`: input `0x20025060`, bias `0x20025030`, kernel
  `0x20024c30`, and output `0x20022c20`. This explains the D trace span and
  also exposes a naming trap: the RTL traced B/horizontal stream starts from the
  input buffer, the A/vertical reuse window starts from the kernel buffer, the
  late A read reaches the input tail (`0x20026c00 + n*0x40`), and the C read
  pair is `0x20025010/0x20025030`, spanning kernel tail plus bias start.
