## Known Local State

- `docs/my_gem5.md` contains the current gem5 test record.
- A previous root-level `my_gem5.md` appears to have been moved or deleted by
  the user; do not restore it unless explicitly asked.
- `test_output.log` records a prior CSR config failure from an `AddrRange`
  string issue in `configs/tutorial/part1/kui_system_csr_test.py`.

## Development Guidance

- Treat `src/sau/reference` as source-of-truth material for comparison, not as
  code to compile into gem5 unless explicitly requested.
- Keep changes to the current gem5 SimObject under `src/sau` scoped and verify
  with the RISCV build or the smallest relevant tutorial config.
- When copying from the external NPU repositories, prefer the provided filelist
  over broad directory copies.
- Preserve the distinction between CSR-triggered functional execution and
  `enable_random_traffic` smoke traffic; the random path is only a connectivity
  check.
- Do not claim full SAU functional equivalence from the current
  GEMM/add/shift/dequant/pointwise/output-transpose/normal-conv/depthwise-conv/
  retain golden vectors; broader mode-specific vectors are still needed,
  especially additional normal/depthwise modes and data shapes, broader mixed
  shift/dequant variants, D_wstrb corner cases, and RTL request-trace
  validation.
